From 416e535d120275dfed7b3068a277f82aa07f0ef7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:36:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: rockchip: rkisp2: Add the HIST_BIG2 stats block

The statistics block table lists HIST_BIG1 twice and leaves the
HIST_BIG2 entry zero-sized, so the third big histogram is written as a
block of size zero that the following AWB block overwrites, and user
space never sees it.

Give HIST_BIG2 its own entry.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
 drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkisp2/rkisp2-stats.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkisp2/rkisp2-stats.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkisp2/rkisp2-stats.c
@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@ rkisp2_stats_blocks_info[] = {
 	RKISP2_STATS_BLOCK_INFO(HIST_LITE, hist),
 	RKISP2_STATS_BLOCK_INFO(HIST_BIG0, hist),
 	RKISP2_STATS_BLOCK_INFO(HIST_BIG1, hist),
-	RKISP2_STATS_BLOCK_INFO(HIST_BIG1, hist),
+	RKISP2_STATS_BLOCK_INFO(HIST_BIG2, hist),
 	RKISP2_STATS_BLOCK_INFO(AWB, awb),
 };
 
